tools.description:
Create or update a Linear document. If `id` is provided, edits the existing document; otherwise creates a new one. When creating, `title` is required, and at most one parent (`project`, `issue`, `initiative`, `cycle`, or `team`) may be specified. Without a parent, pass `private: true` to create the document in your private space. Pass `parentDocument` instead of a parent to create or move the document as a page under another document. Pass `workspace: true` instead of a parent to create or move the document at the workspace level. On update, passing a parent reparents the document. To change parts of the content without resending all of it, pass `patch` instead of `content`.

```ts
mcp__Linear__save_document(args: {
// Document ID or slug to update. Omit to create a new document.
id?: string,
// Document title (required when creating)
title?: string,
// Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. To mention a user, use @displayName (e.g., @johndoe). To embed an image or file, upload it with prepare_file_upload and insert the returned markdown. Besides standard Markdown, Linear accepts: collapsible sections, opened with `>>> Title` (or `+++ Title`) and closed with the same marker on its own line, where `>>> ## Title` makes a collapsible heading; callouts as GitHub alerts, a blockquote whose first line holds only the marker (`> [!NOTE]`, `> [!TIP]`, `> [!IMPORTANT]`, `> [!WARNING]` or `> [!CAUTION]`) and whose next `>` lines hold the text, with an optional `<!-- linear:callout icon=Rocket color=#26b5ce -->` line before the alert for a custom icon (icon name or `:emoji:` code) and hex color; the color must match the alert category (use `> [!NOTE]` with this example), otherwise Linear uses that category's default color; `<linear-date date="2026-11-03" />` for a date; math blocks in a ```math fence or a `$$ … $$` block whose opening `$$` starts a line (inline math is not supported); and the tags that get_document and get_issue return, such as `<user id="…" />` mentions, so content you read can be written back unchanged
content?: string,
// Partial edits applied to the current content, in order and atomically (one failing operation aborts the whole save). Every anchor string must match the current content exactly once. Only valid on update, in place of the full content/description field
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 50
patch?: Array<

 | {
op: "replace",
// Exact text to replace. Must match the current content exactly once
old_string: string, // minLength: 1
// Replacement text. Empty string deletes the match
new_string: string,
// Replace every occurrence instead of requiring a unique match
replace_all?: boolean,
}
 | {
op: "insert_before",
// Exact text to insert before. Must match the current content exactly once
anchor: string, // minLength: 1
// Text to insert directly before the anchor. Include separators (e.g. "\n\n")
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "insert_after",
// Exact text to insert after. Must match the current content exactly once
anchor: string, // minLength: 1
// Text to insert directly after the anchor. Include separators (e.g. "\n\n")
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "prepend",
// Text to insert at the very start of the content
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "append",
// Text to insert at the very end of the content
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "replace_range",
// Exact text where the range starts (inclusive). Must match exactly once
from: string, // minLength: 1
// Exact text where the range ends (exclusive, stays in place). Must match exactly once after `from`
to: string, // minLength: 1
// Text replacing the range. Empty string deletes it
new_string: string,
}

>,
// Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., P-ENG-123), or slug
project?: string,
// Issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123). P-prefixed identifiers (e.g., P-ENG-123) are projects, not issues
issue?: string,
// Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., I-123), or slug
initiative?: string,
// Cycle name, number, or ID. When passing a name or number, also pass `team` to disambiguate.
cycle?: string,
// Team name or ID. Attaches the document to the team, unless `cycle` is also passed, in which case it disambiguates the cycle.
team?: string,
// Icon name or emoji code (e.g. "Rocket" or ":eagle:"), not a raw Unicode emoji
icon?: string,
// Hex color
color?: string,
// true creates the document in your private space, where only you and the people you share it with can see it, or moves an existing document there. To move a private document out, pass a parent instead
private?: boolean,
// Creates the document as a page (sub-document) under this document, or moves an existing document there. The page goes in the same place as its parent document. On update, null moves a page out to the top level of its location. Document ID or slug
parentDocument?: string | null,
// true creates the document at the workspace level, outside any team or project, or moves an existing document there. To move a workspace document out, pass a parent instead
workspace?: boolean,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Create or update a Linear initiative. If `id` is provided, updates the existing initiative; otherwise creates a new one. When creating, `name` is required. To change parts of the description without resending all of it, pass `patch` instead of `description`.

```ts
mcp__Linear__save_initiative(args: {
// Hex color
color?: string,
// Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. To mention a user, use @displayName (e.g., @johndoe)
description?: string,
// Icon name or emoji code (e.g. "Rocket" or ":eagle:"), not a raw Unicode emoji
icon?: string,
// Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., I-123), or slug. If provided, updates the existing initiative
id?: string,
// Label names or IDs as a JSON array of strings (e.g. ["Bug", "Urgent"]). Replaces the full label set; existing labels not included are removed. Omit to leave labels unchanged
labels?: string[],
// Lead team name, key, or ID. Null to remove the lead team
leadTeam?: string | null,
// Initiative name (required when creating)
name?: string,
// User ID, name, email, or "me". Null to remove
owner?: string | null,
// Parent initiatives to add. Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., I-123), or slug. Appended to existing parents
parentInitiatives?: string[],
// Partial edits applied to the current content, in order and atomically (one failing operation aborts the whole save). Every anchor string must match the current content exactly once. Only valid on update, in place of the full content/description field
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 50
patch?: Array<

 | {
// Replacement text. Empty string deletes the match
new_string: string,
// Exact text to replace. Must match the current content exactly once
old_string: string, // minLength: 1
op: "replace",
// Replace every occurrence instead of requiring a unique match
replace_all?: boolean,
}
 | {
// Exact text to insert before. Must match the current content exactly once
anchor: string, // minLength: 1
op: "insert_before",
// Text to insert directly before the anchor. Include separators (e.g. "\n\n")
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
// Exact text to insert after. Must match the current content exactly once
anchor: string, // minLength: 1
op: "insert_after",
// Text to insert directly after the anchor. Include separators (e.g. "\n\n")
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "prepend",
// Text to insert at the very start of the content
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "append",
// Text to insert at the very end of the content
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
// Exact text where the range starts (inclusive). Must match exactly once
from: string, // minLength: 1
// Text replacing the range. Empty string deletes it
new_string: string,
op: "replace_range",
// Exact text where the range ends (exclusive, stays in place). Must match exactly once after `from`
to: string, // minLength: 1
}

>,
// 0=None, 1=Urgent, 2=High, 3=Medium, 4=Low
priority?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 4
// Initiative status (Proposed, Planned, Active, Completed, Canceled)
status?: string,
// Short summary (max 255 chars)
summary?: string,
// Target date (ISO format). Null to remove
targetDate?: string | null,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Create or update a Linear initiative label. If `id` is provided, updates the existing label; otherwise creates a new one. When creating, `name` is required.

```ts
mcp__Linear__save_initiative_label(args: {
// Hex color code
color?: string,
// Label description. Null to clear it
description?: string | null,
// Selection mode for label groups. Defaults to singleSelect when creating; omit to keep it unchanged when updating
groupType?: "singleSelect" | "multiSelect",
// Label name or ID. If provided, updates the existing label
id?: string,
// Whether the label is a group
isGroup?: boolean,
// Label name (required when creating)
name?: string,
// Parent label group name or ID. Null to remove from its group
parent?: string | null,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Create or update a Linear issue. If `id` is provided, updates the existing issue; otherwise creates a new one. When creating, `team` is required, and `title` is required unless `template` is set. Note: use `assignee` (not `assigneeId`) to set the assignee — it accepts a user ID, name, email, or "me".

```ts
mcp__Linear__save_issue(args: {
// Only for updating an existing issue. Pass the issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123). Do NOT pass this parameter when creating a new issue.
id?: string,
// Issue title (required when creating, unless template is set)
title?: string,
// Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. To mention a user, use @displayName (e.g., @johndoe). Besides standard Markdown, Linear accepts: collapsible sections, opened with `>>> Title` (or `+++ Title`) and closed with the same marker on its own line, where `>>> ## Title` makes a collapsible heading; callouts as GitHub alerts, a blockquote whose first line holds only the marker (`> [!NOTE]`, `> [!TIP]`, `> [!IMPORTANT]`, `> [!WARNING]` or `> [!CAUTION]`) and whose next `>` lines hold the text, with an optional `<!-- linear:callout icon=Rocket color=#26b5ce -->` line before the alert for a custom icon (icon name or `:emoji:` code) and hex color; the color must match the alert category (use `> [!NOTE]` with this example), otherwise Linear uses that category's default color; `<linear-date date="2026-11-03" />` for a date; math blocks in a ```math fence or a `$$ … $$` block whose opening `$$` starts a line (inline math is not supported); and the tags that get_document and get_issue return, such as `<user id="…" />` mentions, so content you read can be written back unchanged
description?: string,
// Partial edits applied to the current content, in order and atomically (one failing operation aborts the whole save). Every anchor string must match the current content exactly once. Only valid on update, in place of the full content/description field
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 50
patch?: Array<

 | {
op: "replace",
// Exact text to replace. Must match the current content exactly once
old_string: string, // minLength: 1
// Replacement text. Empty string deletes the match
new_string: string,
// Replace every occurrence instead of requiring a unique match
replace_all?: boolean,
}
 | {
op: "insert_before",
// Exact text to insert before. Must match the current content exactly once
anchor: string, // minLength: 1
// Text to insert directly before the anchor. Include separators (e.g. "\n\n")
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "insert_after",
// Exact text to insert after. Must match the current content exactly once
anchor: string, // minLength: 1
// Text to insert directly after the anchor. Include separators (e.g. "\n\n")
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "prepend",
// Text to insert at the very start of the content
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "append",
// Text to insert at the very end of the content
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "replace_range",
// Exact text where the range starts (inclusive). Must match exactly once
from: string, // minLength: 1
// Exact text where the range ends (exclusive, stays in place). Must match exactly once after `from`
to: string, // minLength: 1
// Text replacing the range. Empty string deletes it
new_string: string,
}

>,
// Team name or ID (required when creating)
team?: string,
// Template name or ID. Applied on create only. The template fills in the content, fields, and sub-issues server-side. A `description` replaces the template body rather than merging with it, but an empty `description` keeps the template body. Labels merge with the template's own
template?: string,
// Cycle name, number, or ID. Null to remove
cycle?: string | null,
// Milestone name or ID
milestone?: string,
// 0=None, 1=Urgent, 2=High, 3=Medium, 4=Low
priority?: number,
// Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., P-ENG-123), or slug. Null to remove
project?: string | null,
// State type, name, or ID
state?: string,
// User ID, name, email, or "me". Null to remove
assignee?: string | null,
// Agent name or ID. When the user asks to delegate to "Linear" or "the Linear agent", this refers to the "Linear" app user specifically. Null to remove
delegate?: string | null,
// Label names or IDs as a JSON array of strings (e.g. ["Bug", "Urgent"]). Replaces the full label set; existing labels not included are removed. Omit to leave labels unchanged. Cannot be combined with addLabels/removeLabels; prefer those for incremental changes
labels?: string[],
// Label names or IDs as a JSON array of strings (e.g. ["Bug", "Urgent"]) to add. Append-only; existing labels are never removed. Cannot be combined with a team change
addLabels?: string[],
// Label names or IDs as a JSON array of strings (e.g. ["Bug", "Urgent"]) to remove. Only valid when updating an existing issue. Cannot be combined with a team change
removeLabels?: string[],
// Due date (ISO format). On update, pass null to remove the due date
dueDate?: string | null,
// ISO-8601 timestamp when the SLA will breach. On update, pass null to remove the SLA
slaBreachesAt?:
 | string // pattern: /^(?:(?:\d\d[2468][048]|\d\d[13579][26]|\d\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\d|2[0-8])))T(?:(?:[01]\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\d:[0-5]\d(?:\.\d+)?(?:Z|([+-](?:[01]\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\d)))$/, format: "date-time"
 | null
,
// SLA day counting type: "all" or "onlyBusinessDays". Only use with slaBreachesAt; null means unset
slaType?: ("all" | "onlyBusinessDays") | null,
// Parent issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123). Null to remove
parentId?: string | null,
// Issue estimate value. On create, pass null or omit for no estimate. On update, pass null to clear the estimate; omitting leaves it unchanged. 0 is a real estimate only on teams that allow zero estimates.
estimate?: number | null,
// Link attachments to add [{url, title}]. Append-only; existing links are never removed
links?: Array<
{
url: string, // format: "uri"
title: string, // minLength: 1
}
>,
// Replace all releases on the issue with these. Cannot be combined with addReleases/removeReleases
setReleases?: string[],
// Release IDs or slugs to add. Append-only; existing releases are never removed
addReleases?: string[],
// Release IDs or slugs to remove. Only valid when updating an existing issue
removeReleases?: string[],
// Issue IDs/identifiers this blocks. Append-only; existing relations are never removed
blocks?: string[],
// Issue IDs/identifiers blocking this. Append-only; existing relations are never removed
blockedBy?: string[],
// Related issue IDs/identifiers. Append-only; existing relations are never removed
relatedTo?: string[],
// Duplicate of issue ID/identifier. Null to remove
duplicateOf?: string | null,
// Issue IDs/identifiers to stop blocking
removeBlocks?: string[],
// Issue IDs/identifiers to remove as blockers of this issue
removeBlockedBy?: string[],
// Related issue IDs/identifiers to remove
removeRelatedTo?: string[],
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Create or update a Linear issue label. If `id` is provided, updates the existing label; otherwise creates a new one. When creating, `name` is required.

```ts
mcp__Linear__save_issue_label(args: {
// Hex color code
color?: string,
// Label description. Null to clear it
description?: string | null,
// Selection mode for label groups. Defaults to singleSelect when creating; omit to keep it unchanged when updating
groupType?: "singleSelect" | "multiSelect",
// Label name or ID. If provided, updates the existing label
id?: string,
// Whether the label is a group
isGroup?: boolean,
// Label name (required when creating)
name?: string,
// Parent label group name or ID. Null to remove from its group
parent?: string | null,
// Team UUID (omit for workspace label). When updating, only disambiguates `id` by name; a label's team cannot be changed
teamId?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Create or update a milestone in a Linear project. If `id` is provided, updates the existing milestone; otherwise creates a new one. When creating, `name` is required.

```ts
mcp__Linear__save_milestone(args: {
// Milestone description
description?: string,
// Milestone name or ID
id?: string,
// Milestone name (required when creating)
name?: string,
// Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., P-ENG-123), or slug
project: string,
// Target completion date (ISO format, null to remove)
targetDate?: string | null,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Create or update a Linear project. If `id` is provided, updates the existing project; otherwise creates a new one. When creating, `name` and at least one team (via `addTeams` or `setTeams`) are required. Pass `template` to create the project from a project template. To change parts of the description without resending all of it, pass `patch` instead of `description`. `state` resolves against the project statuses of the lead team, so pass `leadTeam` when creating a multi-team project whose teams use different statuses.

```ts
mcp__Linear__save_project(args: {
// Initiatives to add. Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., I-123), or slug
addInitiatives?: string[],
// Team name or ID to add
addTeams?: string[],
// Hex color
color?: string,
// Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. To mention a user, use @displayName (e.g., @johndoe). To embed an image or file, upload it with prepare_file_upload and insert the returned markdown
description?: string,
// Icon name or emoji code (e.g. "Rocket" or ":eagle:"), not a raw Unicode emoji
icon?: string,
// Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., P-ENG-123), or slug. If provided, updates the existing project
id?: string,
// Label names or IDs as a JSON array of strings (e.g. ["Bug", "Urgent"]). Replaces the full label set; existing labels not included are removed. Omit to leave labels unchanged
labels?: string[],
// User ID, name, email, or "me". Null to remove, except on create with a template that names a lead
lead?: string | null,
// Team that leads the project. Team name or ID. Overrides the default lead team; added to the project's teams when not among them
leadTeam?: string,
// External resource links to add [{url, title}]. Append-only; existing links are never removed
links?: Array<
{
title: string, // minLength: 1
url: string, // format: "uri"
}
>,
// Project name (required when creating)
name?: string,
// Partial edits applied to the current content, in order and atomically (one failing operation aborts the whole save). Every anchor string must match the current content exactly once. Only valid on update, in place of the full content/description field
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 50
patch?: Array<

 | {
// Replacement text. Empty string deletes the match
new_string: string,
// Exact text to replace. Must match the current content exactly once
old_string: string, // minLength: 1
op: "replace",
// Replace every occurrence instead of requiring a unique match
replace_all?: boolean,
}
 | {
// Exact text to insert before. Must match the current content exactly once
anchor: string, // minLength: 1
op: "insert_before",
// Text to insert directly before the anchor. Include separators (e.g. "\n\n")
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
// Exact text to insert after. Must match the current content exactly once
anchor: string, // minLength: 1
op: "insert_after",
// Text to insert directly after the anchor. Include separators (e.g. "\n\n")
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "prepend",
// Text to insert at the very start of the content
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
op: "append",
// Text to insert at the very end of the content
text: string, // minLength: 1
}
 | {
// Exact text where the range starts (inclusive). Must match exactly once
from: string, // minLength: 1
// Text replacing the range. Empty string deletes it
new_string: string,
op: "replace_range",
// Exact text where the range ends (exclusive, stays in place). Must match exactly once after `from`
to: string, // minLength: 1
}

>,
// 0=None, 1=Urgent, 2=High, 3=Medium, 4=Low
priority?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 4
// Initiatives to remove. Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., I-123), or slug
removeInitiatives?: string[],
// Team name or ID to remove
removeTeams?: string[],
// Replace all initiatives with these. Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., I-123), or slug. Cannot combine with addInitiatives/removeInitiatives
setInitiatives?: string[],
// Replace all teams with these. Cannot combine with addTeams/removeTeams
setTeams?: string[],
// Start date (ISO format). Pair with startDateResolution to indicate precision (e.g. month, quarter). Null to remove
startDate?: string | null,
// Start date resolution. Null for an exact day. When omitted, the current resolution stays and the date snaps to it
startDateResolution?: ("halfYear" | "month" | "quarter" | "year") | null,
// Project status name, type, or ID. Names resolve within the lead team's project statuses. If the lead team is unknown, standard labels resolve as status types; custom names require a status ID or leadTeam
state?: string,
// Short summary (max 255 chars)
summary?: string,
// Target date (ISO format). Pair with targetDateResolution to indicate precision (e.g. month, quarter). Null to remove
targetDate?: string | null,
// Target date resolution. Null for an exact day. When omitted, the current resolution stays and the date snaps to it
targetDateResolution?: ("halfYear" | "month" | "quarter" | "year") | null,
// Template name or ID. Applied on create only. The template fills in the content, fields, and sub-issues server-side. A `description` replaces the template body rather than merging with it, but an empty `description` keeps the template body. Labels merge with the template's own
template?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

