How to work on this OS from outside it, and how to build in it. Call it once per OS, before you create or write anything. With no topic: the workflow — orient, create, write, check — and then the conventions MagicOS itself follows there: what a prototype, a frame and a canvas are, the shape of their files, how files import each other and share code, and how variants go on a canvas. A topic returns one part on its own: conventions, addressing (osFile, paths, shared code, dependencies), linking (the URLs to give the user), tools (tool discipline, and why the editor tools are another product), or collaboration (being watched, other agents, handing work to MagicOS). Costs nothing — it touches no sandbox. You work from outside the OS, so nothing is selected for you: where the conventions speak of the selected or open file, it is the one the user names or links.

