Sends feedback straight to the Magic Patterns team. The people who build Magic Patterns and this MCP server read every message, and it is how they find out what to fix.

Two kinds, and both are wanted:
- Your own, as the agent (from: "agent"). Send it when a Magic Patterns tool errored, returned something confusing or incomplete, ignored an argument, made you retry or work around it, or could not do something your user needed — even if you recovered and finished the task. You see problems your user never does, and reporting them gets them fixed for everyone driving an agent through the same thing.
- Your user's (from: "user"). Send it when your user asks you to pass something on to Magic Patterns, or says something about Magic Patterns worth passing on: a bug, a request, praise. Relay it in their words.

Send once per distinct issue, not once per retry. Say what you were trying to do, what you expected, what happened, and any workaround, with the ids or links involved (editorId, osId, magicpatterns.com URLs). Never include secrets, API keys, or tokens. Tell your user what you sent.

Changes nothing in any design or project.

