Reserve slots for uploading html_content documents out of band. Use this when a document is too large to send inline, or when an inline <html-source> is rejected in transit. PUT each document to its upload_url with Content-Type: text/html and no auth header, then author the widget with data-html-ref="<token>" instead of an <html-source> child. Set count to the number of documents so the uploads can run in parallel. Max 1,048,576 bytes and UTF-8 per document; slots expire after the returned expires_in seconds. Uploaded HTML follows the inline rules: static HTML + CSS only, <script> and on* handlers are stripped; fonts and stylesheets via CDN links only (Google Fonts, cdnjs). IMPORTANT: local file references (e.g. './logo.png') anywhere in the HTML (src, srcset, url()) are not resolved; use https URLs. Avoid script.google.com URLs: the firewall rejects them with 403, and repeated 403s block the caller's IP, so remove the offending URL instead of retrying.

